	// The NPC intro-conversation reply, reconstructed from
	// Captures/account-stricken998-character-dikketest-create-random-actions.json (world conn 37.18.193.22:7012).
	//
	// In that capture the conversation is NOT automatic: the player walks up to the beach NPC and clicks it,
	// sending an Interact (0x642CD3D6, actionType 0x16 = talk-to-NPC). The server then replies with this batch
	// (capture idx 1170-1177): a couple of interact acks, a state block, and the conversation window itself
	// (0x4A3D899A conversation id 12493 + 0xF164A4A5 "remoteformat" id 7615). That is what we send back here so
	// the chat opens only when the player talks to the NPC.
	//
	// The capture's in-world entity handle 0x01316D2B has been substituted to the create-flow temp instance
	// 0x021662C8 (the handle our SpawnPlayer assigns and that the world connection addresses), both in the
	// receiver family tail (C8 C5 D9 10) and in each body's clientInstance field (02 16 62 C8). The player name
	// embedded in the remoteformat XML is still the capture's ("Dikketest"); rebuilding it per-character is a
	// follow-up.
	public partial class GameServerListener
	{
